1	### Task 4: `readingTimeMinutes(text, wpm = 200)`
2	
3	**Files:**
4	- Create: `test/readingTimeMinutes.test.js`
5	- Modify: `src/textstats.js`
6	
7	`readingTimeMinutes` turns a word count into a whole number of minutes. It is the smallest function in the module and depends only on `wordCount`, so it also serves as the check that the three earlier tasks compose.
8	
9	**Behaviour.**
10	
11	- The result is `Math.ceil(wordCount(text) / wpm)`: any text with at least one word takes at least one minute, 200 words take exactly one, 201 words take two, and the empty text takes zero.
12	- `wpm` defaults to 200 when omitted or passed as `undefined`.
13	- `wpm` must be a positive, finite number; fractions such as `150.5` are allowed. Zero, negatives, `NaN`, the infinities and any non-number (including numeric strings and `null`) throw `RangeError` with a message starting `readingTimeMinutes:`.
14	- A non-string `text` throws `TypeError` with a message starting `readingTimeMinutes:`. The text is checked before the rate.
15	- The word count is the same one `wordCount` reports, so hyphenated compounds, contractions and decimals count the way Task 1 defines.
